The upstream development already certifies order 668. That result is prior art.
This adaptation changes the target to order 716, reconstructs different compact
certificate data from the public matrix, recomputes and kernel-checks the
correlation certificates, and adds a bridge to Mathlib's Matrix.IsHadamard.
The adapting applicant used OpenAI Codex. No first-ever formalization or exclusive
entitlement is asserted. The distinct scope and credit allocation require review.

The mathematical matrix was retrieved from the public hoa64 data mirror:
https://github.com/bbeartheancient/hoa64/blob/d825201089123126ce792d4921cba4ae1b8977a3/matrices/hadamard_716.csv.gz
The CSV is data, not a proof trusted by Lean. All reconstructed entries and all
255970 distinct row pairs are independently checked by verify_certificate.py.

Mathlib and Lean retain their own licenses and contributor attributions.
